  "footnote": "All ten courses (at least 30 credits total) require letter grades of C or better. Admission normally requires two philosophy courses of at least 3 credits each with B or better, subject to the Director of Undergraduate Studies. PHIL 2310 is recommended, not required. Honors and the senior thesis are optional: honors normally requires a 3.5 major GPA, 2.7 Cornell GPA, ten philosophy courses of at least 3 credits, two at the 4000/6000 level and four at 3000 or above, plus faculty assessment of substantial writing, class participation and departmental citizenship. Honors excludes PHIL x9xx except PHIL 4900 and PHIL 4901; neither thesis course counts toward the eight core courses. Honors requires advocacy by at least two faculty members; meeting numerical criteria does not guarantee an award. Thesis enrollment requires a faculty advisor; PHIL 4900 and PHIL 4901 are typically taken in consecutive senior terms. Only one level of honors is awarded beginning in 2026-27.",
